external borrowings / high sea sales during first five year period or
any other charges.');
INSERT INTO workflows (section_code, step_index, step_text) VALUES ('6.10', 5, 'It will also include payment made in Indian
Rupees on high sea sales; and
“Inputs” mean raw materials, intermediates, components,
pg.');
INSERT INTO workflows (section_code, step_index, step_text) VALUES ('6.10', 6, 'It will also include payment made in Indian
Rupees on high sea sales; and
“Inputs” mean raw materials, intermediates, components,
consumables, parts and packing materials.');
INSERT INTO workflows (section_code, step_index, step_text) VALUES ('6.10', 7, '(b) If any goods are obtained from another EOU / EHTP / STP / BTP /
SEZ unit, or procured from an international exhibition held in India,
or bonded warehouses or precious metals procured from
nominated agencies, value of such goods shall be included under
“B”.');
INSERT INTO workflows (section_code, step_index, step_text) VALUES ('6.10', 8, '(d) For annual calculation of NFE, value of imported capital goods and
lump sum payment of foreign technical know-how fee shall be
amortized as under: 1st– 10th year: 10%.');
INSERT INTO workflows (section_code, step_index, step_text) VALUES ('6.10', 9, 'Run validation: 6.10 Net Foreign Exchange (NFE) Earnings
(a) EOU / EHTP / STP / BTP unit shall be a positive net foreign
exchange earner.');
INSERT INTO workflows (section_code, step_index, step_text) VALUES ('6.10', 10, 'Run validation: NFE earnings shall be calculated cumulatively in
the block period as per Paragraph 6.04 of FTP, according to the
formula given below.');
INSERT INTO workflows (section_code, step_index, step_text) VALUES ('6.10', 11, 'Run validation: Items of manufacture for export specified in
Lo P / Lo I alone shall be taken into account for calculation of NFE.');
INSERT INTO workflows (section_code, step_index, step_text) VALUES ('6.10', 12, 'Handle exception: Provided that above
amortization rates would be applicable only if an undertaking is
given by a unit that it will not exit to DTA in the first 10 years.');
